{
  "title": "Matrix5.2",
  "notes": [
    "<h2>Determinant Proofs using Properties (Question 6)</h2>",
    "<h3>i) Proof</h3>",
    "$$\\begin{vmatrix} 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ a & b & c \\\\ bc & ca & ab \\end{vmatrix} = (a-b)(b-c)(c-a)$$",
    "<p><b>Proof:</b></p>",
    "$$\\text{LHS} = \\begin{vmatrix} 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ a & b & c \\\\ bc & ca & ab \\end{vmatrix}$$",
    "<p>Applying column operations $C_1 \\to C_1 - C_2$ and $C_2 \\to C_2 - C_3$:</p>",
    "$$= \\begin{vmatrix} 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ a-b & b-c & c \\\\ bc-ca & ca-ab & ab \\end{vmatrix}$$",
    "$$= \\begin{vmatrix} 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ a-b & b-c & c \\\\ -c(a-b) & -a(b-c) & ab \\end{vmatrix}$$",
    "<p>Taking $(a-b)$ common from $C_1$ and $(b-c)$ common from $C_2$:</p>",
    "$$= (a-b)(b-c) \\begin{vmatrix} 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & c \\\\ -c & -a & ab \\end{vmatrix}$$",
    "<p>Expanding along Row 1 ($R_1$):</p>",
    "$$= (a-b)(b-c) \\cdot 1 \\cdot \\begin{vmatrix} 1 & 1 \\\\ -c & -a \\end{vmatrix}$$",
    "$$= (a-b)(b-c)[-a - (-c)]$$",
    "$$= (a-b)(b-c)(c-a) = \\text{RHS}$$",
    "<h3>ii) Proof</h3>",
    "$$\\begin{vmatrix} a & b & c \\\\ a^2 & b^2 & c^2 \\\\ b+c & c+a & a+b \\end{vmatrix} = (b-c)(c-a)(a-b)(a+b+c)$$",
    "<p><b>Proof:</b></p>",
    "$$\\text{LHS} = \\begin{vmatrix} a & b & c \\\\ a^2 & b^2 & c^2 \\\\ b+c & c+a & a+b \\end{vmatrix}$$",
    "<p>Applying $R_3 \\to R_3 + R_1$:</p>",
    "$$= \\begin{vmatrix} a & b & c \\\\ a^2 & b^2 & c^2 \\\\ a+b+c & a+b+c & a+b+c \\end{vmatrix}$$",
    "<p>Taking $(a+b+c)$ common from $R_3$:</p>",
    "$$= (a+b+c) \\begin{vmatrix} a & b & c \\\\ a^2 & b^2 & c^2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 \\end{vmatrix}$$",
    "<p>Applying $C_1 \\to C_1 - C_2$ and $C_2 \\to C_2 - C_3$:</p>",
    "$$= (a+b+c) \\begin{vmatrix} a-b & b-c & c \\\\ a^2-b^2 & b^2-c^2 & c^2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\end{vmatrix}$$",
    "<p>Taking $(a-b)$ common from $C_1$ and $(b-c)$ common from $C_2$:</p>",
    "$$= (a+b+c)(a-b)(b-c) \\begin{vmatrix} 1 & 1 & c \\\\ a+b & b+c & c^2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\end{vmatrix}$$",
    "<p>Expanding along $R_3$:</p>",
    "$$= (a+b+c)(a-b)(b-c) [(b+c) - (a+b)]$$",
    "$$= (b-c)(c-a)(a-b)(a+b+c) = \\text{RHS}$$",
    "<h3>iii) Proof</h3>",
    "$$\\begin{vmatrix} 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ a & b & c \\\\ a^3 & b^3 & c^3 \\end{vmatrix} = (b-c)(c-a)(a-b)(a+b+c)$$",
    "<p><b>Proof:</b></p>",
    "$$\\text{LHS} = \\begin{vmatrix} 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ a & b & c \\\\ a^3 & b^3 & c^3 \\end{vmatrix}$$",
    "<p>Applying $C_1 \\to C_1 - C_2$ and $C_2 \\to C_2 - C_3$:</p>",
    "$$= \\begin{vmatrix} 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ a-b & b-c & c \\\\ a^3-b^3 & b^3-c^3 & c^3 \\end{vmatrix}$$",
    "<p>Factoring $x^3 - y^3 = (x-y)(x^2 + xy + y^2)$, take $(a-b)$ common from $C_1$ and $(b-c)$ common from $C_2$:</p>",
    "$$= (a-b)(b-c) \\begin{vmatrix} 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & c \\\\ a^2+ab+b^2 & b^2+bc+c^2 & c^3 \\end{vmatrix}$$",
    "<p>Expanding along $R_1$:</p>",
    "$$= (a-b)(b-c) [(b^2+bc+c^2) - (a^2+ab+b^2)]$$",
    "$$= (a-b)(b-c) [bc - ab + c^2 - a^2]$$",
    "$$= (a-b)(b-c) [b(c-a) + (c-a)(c+a)]$$",
    "$$= (a-b)(b-c)(c-a)(a+b+c) = (b-c)(c-a)(a-b)(a+b+c) = \\text{RHS}$$",
    "<h3>iv) Proof</h3>",
    "$$\\begin{vmatrix} x & y & z \\\\ x^2 & y^2 & z^2 \\\\ yz & zx & xy \\end{vmatrix} = (y-z)(z-x)(x-y)(yz+zx+xy)$$",
    "<p><b>Proof:</b></p>",
    "$$\\text{LHS} = \\begin{vmatrix} x & y & z \\\\ x^2 & y^2 & z^2 \\\\ yz & zx & xy \\end{vmatrix}$$",
    "<p>Multiply $R_1, R_2, R_3$ by $x, y, z$ respectively and divide by $xyz$:</p>",
    "$$= \\frac{1}{xyz} \\begin{vmatrix} x^2 & y^2 & z^2 \\\\ x^3 & y^3 & z^3 \\\\ xyz & xyz & xyz \\end{vmatrix}$$",
    "<p>Taking $xyz$ common from $R_3$:</p>",
    "$$= \\frac{xyz}{xyz} \\begin{vmatrix} x^2 & y^2 & z^2 \\\\ x^3 & y^3 & z^3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 \\end{vmatrix}$$",
    "$$= \\begin{vmatrix} 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ x^2 & y^2 & z^2 \\\\ x^3 & y^3 & z^3 \\end{vmatrix}$$",
    "<p>Applying $C_1 \\to C_1 - C_2$ and $C_2 \\to C_2 - C_3$:</p>",
    "$$= \\begin{vmatrix} 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ x^2-y^2 & y^2-z^2 & z^2 \\\\ x^3-y^3 & y^3-z^3 & z^3 \\end{vmatrix}$$",
    "<p>Taking $(x-y)$ from $C_1$ and $(y-z)$ from $C_2$:</p>",
    "$$= (x-y)(y-z) \\begin{vmatrix} 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ x+y & y+z & z^2 \\\\ x^2+xy+y^2 & y^2+yz+z^2 & z^3 \\end{vmatrix}$$",
    "<p>Expanding along $R_1$:</p>",
    "$$= (x-y)(y-z) [(x+y)(y^2+yz+z^2) - (y+z)(x^2+xy+y^2)]$$",
    "$$= (x-y)(y-z) [xz^2 - x^2z + yz^2 - x^2y]$$",
    "$$= (x-y)(y-z) [xz(z-x) + y(z^2-x^2)]$$",
    "$$= (y-z)(z-x)(x-y)(yz+zx+xy) = \\text{RHS}$$",
    "<h3>v) Proof</h3>",
    "$$\\begin{vmatrix} b+c & a & b \\\\ c+a & c & a \\\\ a+b & b & c \\end{vmatrix} = (a+b+c)(a-c)^2$$",
    "<p><b>Proof:</b></p>",
    "$$\\text{LHS} = \\begin{vmatrix} b+c & a & b \\\\ c+a & c & a \\\\ a+b & b & c \\end{vmatrix}$$",
    "<p>Applying $C_1 \\to C_1 - C_2 - C_3$:</p>",
    "$$= \\begin{vmatrix} (b+c)-a-b & a & b \\\\ (c+a)-c-a & c & a \\\\ (a+b)-b-c & b & c \\end{vmatrix}$$",
    "$$= \\begin{vmatrix} c-a & a & b \\\\ 0 & c & a \\\\ -(c-a) & b & c \\end{vmatrix}$$",
    "<p>Taking $(c-a)$ common from $C_1$:</p>",
    "$$= (c-a) \\begin{vmatrix} 1 & a & b \\\\ 0 & c & a \\\\ -1 & b & c \\end{vmatrix}$$",
    "<p>Applying $R_3 \\to R_3 + R_1$:</p>",
    "$$= (c-a) \\begin{vmatrix} 1 & a & b \\\\ 0 & c & a \\\\ 0 & a+b & b+c \\end{vmatrix}$$",
    "<p>Expanding along $C_1$:</p>",
    "$$= (c-a) [c(b+c) - a(a+b)]$$",
    "$$= (c-a) [bc + c^2 - a^2 - ab]$$",
    "$$= (c-a) [(c^2 - a^2) + b(c - a)]$$",
    "$$= (c-a)(c-a) (c + a + b) = (a+b+c)(a-c)^2 = \\text{RHS}$$",
    "<h3>vi) Proof</h3>",
    "$$\\begin{vmatrix} a-b-c & 2a & 2a \\\\ 2b & b-c-a & 2b \\\\ 2c & 2c & c-a-b \\end{vmatrix} = (a+b+c)^3$$",
    "<p><b>Proof:</b></p>",
    "$$\\text{LHS} = \\begin{vmatrix} a-b-c & 2a & 2a \\\\ 2b & b-c-a & 2b \\\\ 2c & 2c & c-a-b \\end{vmatrix}$$",
    "<p>Applying $R_1 \\to R_1 + R_2 + R_3$:</p>",
    "$$= \\begin{vmatrix} a+b+c & a+b+c & a+b+c \\\\ 2b & b-c-a & 2b \\\\ 2c & 2c & c-a-b \\end{vmatrix}$$",
    "<p>Taking $(a+b+c)$ common from $R_1$:</p>",
    "$$= (a+b+c) \\begin{vmatrix} 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2b & b-c-a & 2b \\\\ 2c & 2c & c-a-b \\end{vmatrix}$$",
    "<p>Applying $C_2 \\to C_2 - C_1$ and $C_3 \\to C_3 - C_1$:</p>",
    "$$= (a+b+c) \\begin{vmatrix} 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2b & -(a+b+c) & 0 \\\\ 2c & 0 & -(a+b+c) \\end{vmatrix}$$",
    "<p>Expanding along $R_1$:</p>",
    "$$= (a+b+c) \\cdot [-(a+b+c) \\cdot -(a+b+c) - 0] = (a+b+c)^3 = \\text{RHS}$$",
    "<h3>vii) Proof</h3>",
    "$$\\begin{vmatrix} 1+a_1 & a_2 & a_3 \\\\ a_1 & 1+a_2 & a_3 \\\\ a_1 & a_2 & 1+a_3 \\end{vmatrix} = 1 + a_1 + a_2 + a_3$$",
    "<p><b>Proof:</b></p>",
    "$$\\text{LHS} = \\begin{vmatrix} 1+a_1 & a_2 & a_3 \\\\ a_1 & 1+a_2 & a_3 \\\\ a_1 & a_2 & 1+a_3 \\end{vmatrix}$$",
    "<p>Applying $C_1 \\to C_1 + C_2 + C_3$:</p>",
    "$$= \\begin{vmatrix} 1+a_1+a_2+a_3 & a_2 & a_3 \\\\ 1+a_1+a_2+a_3 & 1+a_2 & a_3 \\\\ 1+a_1+a_2+a_3 & a_2 & 1+a_3 \\end{vmatrix}$$",
    "<p>Taking $(1+a_1+a_2+a_3)$ common from $C_1$:</p>",
    "$$= (1+a_1+a_2+a_3) \\begin{vmatrix} 1 & a_2 & a_3 \\\\ 1 & 1+a_2 & a_3 \\\\ 1 & a_2 & 1+a_3 \\end{vmatrix}$$",
    "<p>Applying $R_2 \\to R_2 - R_1$ and $R_3 \\to R_3 - R_1$:</p>",
    "$$= (1+a_1+a_2+a_3) \\begin{vmatrix} 1 & a_2 & a_3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\end{vmatrix}$$",
    "<p>Expanding along $C_1$:</p>",
    "$$= (1+a_1+a_2+a_3) \\cdot (1 - 0) = 1 + a_1 + a_2 + a_3 = \\text{RHS}$$",
    "<h3>viii) Proof</h3>",
    "$$\\begin{vmatrix} 1+x & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1+y & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1+z \\end{vmatrix} = xyz \\left( \\frac{1}{x} + \\frac{1}{y} + \\frac{1}{z} + 1 \\right)$$",
    "<p><b>Proof:</b></p>",
    "$$\\text{LHS} = \\begin{vmatrix} 1+x & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1+y & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1+z \\end{vmatrix}$$",
    "<p>Factor out $x$ from $R_1$, $y$ from $R_2$, and $z$ from $R_3$:</p>",
    "$$= xyz \\begin{vmatrix} \\frac{1}{x} + 1 & \\frac{1}{x} & \\frac{1}{x} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & \\frac{1}{y} + 1 & \\frac{1}{y} \\\\ \\frac{1}{z} & \\frac{1}{z} & \\frac{1}{z} + 1 \\end{vmatrix}$$",
    "<p>Applying $R_1 \\to R_1 + R_2 + R_3$:</p>",
    "$$= xyz \\begin{vmatrix} 1 + \\frac{1}{x} + \\frac{1}{y} + \\frac{1}{z} & 1 + \\frac{1}{x} + \\frac{1}{y} + \\frac{1}{z} & 1 + \\frac{1}{x} + \\frac{1}{y} + \\frac{1}{z} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & \\frac{1}{y} + 1 & \\frac{1}{y} \\\\ \\frac{1}{z} & \\frac{1}{z} & \\frac{1}{z} + 1 \\end{vmatrix}$$",
    "<p>Taking $\\left(1 + \\frac{1}{x} + \\frac{1}{y} + \\frac{1}{z}\\right)$ common from $R_1$:</p>",
    "$$= xyz \\left(1 + \\frac{1}{x} + \\frac{1}{y} + \\frac{1}{z}\\right) \\begin{vmatrix} 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & \\frac{1}{y} + 1 & \\frac{1}{y} \\\\ \\frac{1}{z} & \\frac{1}{z} & \\frac{1}{z} + 1 \\end{vmatrix}$$",
    "<p>Applying $C_2 \\to C_2 - C_1$ and $C_3 \\to C_3 - C_1$:</p>",
    "$$= xyz \\left(1 + \\frac{1}{x} + \\frac{1}{y} + \\frac{1}{z}\\right) \\begin{vmatrix} 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & 1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{z} & 0 & 1 \\end{vmatrix}$$",
    "<p>Expanding along $R_1$:</p>",
    "$$= xyz \\left(\\frac{1}{x} + \\frac{1}{y} + \\frac{1}{z} + 1\\right) \\cdot (1 - 0) = xyz \\left(\\frac{1}{x} + \\frac{1}{y} + \\frac{1}{z} + 1\\right) = \\text{RHS}$$"
  ]
}
